      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.4731463+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.59]     a member increment reads the member as text, counts a missing or empty one as zero, keeps the other members and refuses a member that is not an integer, changing nothing [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.4731644+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.59]     a numeric comparison is exact on PostgreSQL and IEEE double on SQLite, so two integers that differ past 2^53 compare equal only on SQLite [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.4731864+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.59]     a key is a member name and never a path: dots, dollars, brackets, quotes, spaces, the empty name and non-ASCII names match only the member of that exact name [SKIP]</Text>
