      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.4732039+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.59]     unicode survives the round trip: an escaped and a raw spelling are the same text, keys and values match, a surrogate pair is one character, and the stored text is not escaped [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.4732346+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.59]     an equality on a key states how it compares: text matches the text, a number matches 10, 10.0, "1e1" and hex text alike, a boolean matches yes and 1 [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.4732533+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.59]     a member that is not an integer, a fraction, a word or a value past int32, makes the increment fail and leaves the document as it was [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.5043141+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.63]     a unit of work that is not committed leaves nothing behind, and one that commits keeps its rows [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.5236135+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.65]     an exclusive named lock keeps a second unit of work out until the first commits, and a shared one admits shared holders only [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.5253555+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.65]     insert-many splits across statements at the provider's bind limit and stores every row exactly once [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.5273080+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.66]     a session lease is held by one caller at a time and released on disposal, or refused before any connection is opened [SKIP]</Text>
