      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.5671420+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.70]     a row lock inside a unit of work serialises read-modify-write, so concurrent increments lose nothing [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.6329765+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.76]     like matching is case sensitive and the ignore-case forms match any case, as in PostgreSQL [SKIP]</Text>
      </RunInfo>
      <RunInfo computerName="b21f193f5bd8" outcome="Warning" timestamp="2026-11-26T15:33:28.6554732+00:00">
        <Text>[xUnit.net 00:02:33.78]     a delete is soft: the row leaves live reads, stays in the trash, and a restore brings it back [SKIP]</Text>
